### (1/3) Make modifier handling testable

**Severity:** `medium`

If a Windows key is held when this right-lock release injects Escape, the keystroke becomes Win+Esc, which turns Magnifier off. Factor the decision into a pure helper so both Windows keys can be verified alongside Ctrl and Alt.

```suggestion
    };

    constexpr bool ShouldInjectEscape(bool controlDown, bool altDown, bool leftWindowsKeyDown, bool rightWindowsKeyDown)
    {
        return !controlDown && !altDown && !leftWindowsKeyDown && !rightWindowsKeyDown;
    }
```

### (2/3) Cover both Windows keys

**Severity:** `medium`

Add deterministic coverage for either Windows key, in addition to Ctrl and Alt, so the guard cannot regress on one side of the keyboard.

```suggestion
    TEST_CLASS(ContextMenuDismissal)
    {
    public:
        TEST_METHOD(EscapeIsInjectedWithoutModifiers)
        {
            Assert::IsTrue(ShouldInjectEscape(false, false, false, false));
        }

        TEST_METHOD(EscapeIsSkippedWhileModifiersAreHeld)
        {
            Assert::IsFalse(ShouldInjectEscape(true, false, false, false));
            Assert::IsFalse(ShouldInjectEscape(false, true, false, false));
            Assert::IsFalse(ShouldInjectEscape(false, false, true, false));
            Assert::IsFalse(ShouldInjectEscape(false, false, false, true));
        }
    };

    TEST_CLASS(HoldToLock)
```

### (3/3) Guard the Escape injection

**Severity:** `medium`

Before sending Escape, check Ctrl, Alt, and both Windows keys and return when any is down. This keeps the context menu open rather than injecting a shortcut such as Win+Esc, which turns Magnifier off.

```suggestion
            const bool controlDown = (GetAsyncKeyState(VK_CONTROL) & 0x8000) != 0;
            const bool altDown = (GetAsyncKeyState(VK_MENU) & 0x8000) != 0;
            const bool leftWindowsKeyDown = (GetAsyncKeyState(VK_LWIN) & 0x8000) != 0;
            const bool rightWindowsKeyDown = (GetAsyncKeyState(VK_RWIN) & 0x8000) != 0;
            if (!mousebuttonlock::ShouldInjectEscape(controlDown, altDown, leftWindowsKeyDown, rightWindowsKeyDown))
            {
                return;
            }

            INPUT keys[2]{};
```
